messages:
maya: Heads-up — intermittent hangs in integration where we stream model responses from the hosted API. Seen in Windows CI and a couple local dev runs. Repro steps below.

maya: Minimal repro: we call client.GetStreamAsync(url) then copy to Response.Body with CopyToAsync. When Polly retry kicks in it seems to hang or throw 'The response content stream is not readable'.

maya: Code snippet:```csharp
using var resp = await httpClient.SendAsync(req, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead);
using var stream = await resp.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
await stream.CopyToAsync(response.Body, 81920, cancellationToken);
```

liam: Are we disposing HttpClient per request? That can cause weird connection resets. We should use IHttpClientFactory and singleton HttpClient instances.

nishant: Also likely related to Polly retry + non-buffered content. If a request fails after the server started streaming, the original request's HttpContent (or response stream) can't be replayed. Polly will try to re-execute the delegate but the request/stream is already consumed.

sam: Two quick fixes: 1) buffer request content for retries (if payload small) or 2) make retries only for idempotent GETs or those with checkpointed side effects. For streaming responses, prefer not to retry at middleware level.

nishant: Example clone approach for request body (for small bodies):```csharp
HttpRequestMessage Clone(HttpRequestMessage req) {
  var clone = new HttpRequestMessage(req.Method, req.RequestUri);
  if (req.Content != null) {
    var bytes = await req.Content.ReadAsByteArrayAsync();
    clone.Content = new ByteArrayContent(bytes);
    foreach (var h in req.Content.Headers) clone.Content.Headers.TryAddWithoutValidation(h.Key, h.Value);
  }
  foreach (var h in req.Headers) clone.Headers.TryAddWithoutValidation(h.Key, h.Value);
  return clone;
}
```
But caveat: not great for large payloads.

liam: Another pattern is to have the retry policy only around the SendAsync level but not include the downstream stream consumption. Use ResponseHeadersRead to accept the response, then if status >=400 treat as retryable, otherwise stream out without wrapping stream consumption in retry.

olivia: For server-side streaming from the model, if the SDK exposes a streaming reader, the client should be the one to decide retry boundaries. Maybe add an explicit Idempotency header so downstream can detect duplicates.

maya: The tests that flake are our long-poll streams where we hit a transient network blip and Polly retries; sometimes the original task never completes and we get stuck waiting on CopyToAsync.

sam: On CopyToAsync hangs, ensure you pass the cancellation token through and that the response stream is read with ResponseHeadersRead. Example:```csharp
using var resp = await httpClient.SendAsync(req, HttpCompletionOption.ResponseHeadersRead, ct);
using var stream = await resp.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
await stream.CopyToAsync(targetStream, 81920, ct);
```
If the token cancels, CopyToAsync will stop.

nishant: Also check ServicePointManager.DefaultConnectionLimit or SocketsHttpHandler.MaxConnectionsPerServer — hitting connection limit can cause queueing that looks like a hang. For dotnet core use:```csharp
new SocketsHttpHandler { MaxConnectionsPerServer = 100 }
```

liam: Quick policy suggestion: wrap SendAsync in Polly but exclude streaming consumption. Pseudocode:```csharp
var resp = await retryPolicy.ExecuteAsync(() => httpClient.SendAsync(req, ResponseHeadersRead));
if (!resp.IsSuccessStatusCode) throw;
using var stream = await resp.Content.ReadAsStreamAsync();
await ConsumeStream(stream); // no retry here
```

maya: Thanks — does anyone want to take a quick PR to change client behaviour? I can open one but maybe liam you already have a branch.

liam: I have a branch that switches to IHttpClientFactory + ResponseHeadersRead and moves Polly to only cover SendAsync. I'll push and tag for review in a bit. Please review api-client/issue-452 branch when up.

ci-bot: CI: integration/azure-win-stream-tests failed 3/5 — retrying pipeline per flaky test policy. (build/4567)

olivia: If we change retry behavior, add an e2e test that simulates a transient DNS drop mid-request and confirm the client surfaces an error instead of hanging.

maya: Action items: liam push branch; add e2e for transient blip; nishant add note in SDK docs about streaming + retry semantics; sam to review CopyToAsync cancellation path.

maya: Thanks all :thumbsup:
